    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0049" n="37" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/10–940: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-09T13:00:00-03:00">October 9, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 9—11:44 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>476. For the Under Secretary. Department’s 236, October 8, 7 p.m.<anchor n="47"
                        xml:id="d37-f1"/> On September 27 Christian and Brereton were asked to meet
                    two Argentine naval captains in order to consider the agenda. On October 4 the
                    conversations opened between our officers and senior officers of the Argentine
                    Army and Navy. Christian and Brereton are satisfied with the interest shown in
                    these informal talks which they consider are progressing slowly but
                    satisfactorily.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d37-f1" n="47" xml:id="d37-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Department inquired whether any date had been fixed for staff
                    conversations (810.20 Defense/9–2540).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
